From: LECH OS <dev@lech-os.invalid>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Use no location assistance servers outside an emergency

LECH OS sends no data to location assistance servers of third parties
by default. On the Pixel 9 the carrier settings name supl.google.com
for SUPL (A-GPS) and 1.ssiloc.com (Samsung) for the satellite
predictions (PSDS); both were contacted at every start (network audit,
7. 11. 2026). Outside an emergency there is no SUPL (localhost,
SUPL_MODE 0). The satellite predictions (PSDS) of the Samsung GNSS chip
come from the cache of GrapheneOS (samsung.psds.grapheneos.org, as on
GrapheneOS) instead of Samsung: without any PSDS the Pixel 9 found no
position outdoors (13. 11. 2026). Other PSDS servers are removed. In an emergency the
configuration of the vendor and the carrier is kept, so a call to 112
gets a fast location. Servers of LECH OS can take their place later.
---
 .../location/gnss/GnssConfiguration.java      | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/location/gnss/GnssConfiguration.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/location/gnss/GnssConfiguration.java
index 04b11c0..0559bde 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/location/gnss/GnssConfiguration.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/location/gnss/GnssConfiguration.java
@@ -294,6 +294,9 @@ public class GnssConfiguration {
          */
         loadPropertiesFromGpsDebugConfig(mProperties, DEBUG_PROPERTIES_VENDOR_FILE);
         loadPropertiesFromGpsDebugConfig(mProperties, DEBUG_PROPERTIES_SYSTEM_FILE);
+        if (!inEmergency) {
+            removeAssistanceServers(mProperties);
+        }
         mEsExtensionSec = getRangeCheckedConfigEsExtensionSec();
 
         logConfigurations();
@@ -346,6 +349,36 @@ public class GnssConfiguration {
         }
     }
 
+    /**
+     * LECH OS: no location assistance servers outside an emergency. The vendor files and the
+     * carrier settings name servers of third parties (on the Pixel 9 supl.google.com for SUPL and
+     * 1.ssiloc.com of Samsung for PSDS), which learn the IP address, the time and the cell of the
+     * phone. No SUPL (the server is localhost, SUPL_MODE 0). The satellite predictions (PSDS) of
+     * the Samsung GNSS chip come from the cache of GrapheneOS instead of Samsung (as on GrapheneOS:
+     * https://grapheneos.org/faq, "samsung.psds.grapheneos.org ... a cache of Samsung's data"); they
+     * carry nothing about the phone and shorten the first fix from minutes to seconds (Pixel 9:
+     * no fix outdoors without them, 13. 11. 2026). Other PSDS servers are removed. In an emergency
+     * the configuration of the vendor and the carrier is kept. Servers of LECH OS can take their
+     * place later.
+     */
+    private static final String SAMSUNG_PSDS_CACHE = "samsung.psds.grapheneos.org";
+
+    private static void removeAssistanceServers(Properties properties) {
+        properties.setProperty(CONFIG_SUPL_HOST, "localhost");
+        properties.setProperty(CONFIG_SUPL_MODE, "0");
+        for (String key : new String[] {CONFIG_LONGTERM_PSDS_SERVER_1, CONFIG_LONGTERM_PSDS_SERVER_2,
+                CONFIG_LONGTERM_PSDS_SERVER_3, CONFIG_NORMAL_PSDS_SERVER,
+                CONFIG_REALTIME_PSDS_SERVER}) {
+            String server = properties.getProperty(key);
+            if (server != null && server.matches("https?://([0-9a-z-]+\\.)*ssiloc\\.com/.*")) {
+                properties.setProperty(key,
+                        server.replaceFirst("^https?://[^/]+", "https://" + SAMSUNG_PSDS_CACHE));
+            } else {
+                properties.remove(key);
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
     private void logConfigurations() {
         FrameworkStatsLog.write(FrameworkStatsLog.GNSS_CONFIGURATION_REPORTED,
                 getSuplHost(),
